-# OMP (hoshi-omp) plugin development
+# Oh My Pi extension development
 
-## Dependencies and versions
+This is the OMP port of the Hoshi plugin-development workflow. Invoke it with `read skill://opencode-plugin-dev/SKILL.md`.
 
-- OMP (hoshi-omp) does **not** install dependencies for local plugin packages. A
-  missing install shows up as `Cannot find package '@opencode/plugin'` in
-  `~/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log` and the plugin reports
-  `failed`. Run `bun install` at the workspace root after any `package.json`
-  change.
-- Pin `@opencode/plugin` (and `@opencode/client`) to the **installed**
-  OpenCode version (`opencode --version`) in every package. Mixed pins mean
-  mixed API types and runtime behaviour.
-- Read the real `.d.ts` files under `node_modules/.bun/@opencode+plugin@<v>*/`
-  before relying on an API. Types and runtime can drift: for example 2.0.20
-  exposes `ctx.catalog` where the types declare `ctx.model`; support both.
+## Use the installed host contract
 
-## Live servers hot-reload plugin code
+- Read the pinned version from `package.json` and the installed `node_modules/@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent/src/` and `dist/types/`. OpenCode's `Plugin.define`, tool transforms, RPC and TUI plugin APIs do not apply.
+- Extensions export a default factory receiving `ExtensionAPI`. Register handlers/tools/commands in the factory; defer session-dependent work until lifecycle handlers. Registration and live session action APIs have different lifetimes.
+- Registered extension tools use `execute(toolCallId, params, signal, onUpdate, ctx)`. MCP/custom-tool internals use a different argument order; inspect the specific interface before invoking it.
+- Return `content: [{ type: "text", text }]` with optional `details`, and propagate the invocation's cancellation signal.
 
-- A running `opencode serve` watches local plugin files and reloads the plugin
-  **into live sessions** as soon as a file changes. Editing plugin source is a
-  live change for anyone using that server.
-- While the user is working, batch edits, keep each save valid (typecheck
-  first), and verify the live state afterwards.
-- A reload rebuilds agents and models by replaying transforms in registration
-  order, and the host's config layer (`opencode.config.agent`,
-  `opencode.config.provider`) can re-register **after** your plugin. If your
-  transform must win (for example setting agent models), detect it — your
-  transform sees agents defined in `agents/*.md` missing — then re-register
-  your transform and call `ctx.agent.reload()`, with a bounded retry count.
+## Registration and discovery
 
-## Logs and verification
+- Hoshi's `scripts/setup.ts` writes extension paths into `.runtime/omp/agent/config.yml`. Add the source registration, run setup and verify the actual loader. Creating an extension file alone does not register it.
+- Persist settings in `config/` and agent material in `agent/`. `.runtime/` contains generated settings, credentials and sessions. Resolve paths from the module or `HOSHI_OMP_ROOT`; temporary paths must not enter installed configuration.
+- Settings arrays replace lower-precedence arrays. A project's extension list can replace a global list, so verify the effective list in the relevant project.
+- `--no-extensions` disables ambient discovery; explicit extension arguments have their own semantics. Do not infer launcher behavior from a standalone registration test.
+- Built-in command names are reserved. Use a Hoshi command name where necessary and verify the registered command list.
+- Source edits are not a guarantee of live module reload. Inspect the installed extension-loading contract, and do not restart a user's running session to make an edit take effect without authorization.
 
-- In service mode (`opencode serve --service`) plugin `console.*` output is
-  not visible anywhere. Write important events (applied changes, validation
-  errors with `file:line:col`, recoveries) to your own small log file under
-  `$XDG_STATE_HOME/opencode/` and never throw if it can't be written.
-- Verify without model calls:
-  - `opencode api GET /api/plugin` — every plugin's `active`/`failed` state
-    and error ref (details in the server log).
-  - `opencode api GET /api/agent`, `/api/skill`, `/api/command`,
-    `/api/config` — effective agents and models, discovered skills and
-    commands, resolved config (including `{env:VAR}` expansion).
-  - `opencode api POST /api/location/reload` — force a reload.
-- `opencode api` starts the background service if none is running. Stop only
-  what you started (track the PID); never `pkill` by pattern while the user
-  may have a session open.
-- For runtime tests that need a real host, start a **private** server:
-  isolated `HOME`/`XDG_*`/`TMPDIR` under a scratch directory, its own port,
-  a scratch config registering only the plugin under test. Never touch the
-  user's config or service.
+## Session and permission boundaries
 
-## Registration and config
+- Factories are rebound to subagent sessions. Use `ctx.agent.kind` for main/child scope and trusted `ctx.agent.name` for the child role. Task depth zero is not equivalent to a main session.
+- Keep state scoped to its owning session. Reconstruct durable state from the current branch after resume or session changes; never reuse another session's cache, pruning decisions, role or warnings.
+- Hoshi authorizes executions in `extensions/permissions.ts`. New tools need an explicit mapping and tests in `lib/permissions.ts`; appearing in a catalog does not prove a call is allowed.
+- `tool_call` may block or revise input. Authorize the actual execution arguments and test indirect dispatch as well as direct calls. Model-authored claims are not caller identity.
+- Provider payload hooks must match both provider and API. Preserve unrelated fields and verify serialized requests with a fake transport. Changing a global thinking level does not prove that the request currently being sent changed.
 
-- Register local packages in `opencode.json` `plugins` as
-  `{ "package": "./packages/<name>", "options": { … } }`; validate options at
-  load and fail with a message naming the bad option.
-- Paths in options: use `{env:HOME}` rather than absolute user paths.
-- Keep plugin-owned data files (for example YAML presets) outside
-  `opencode.json`, re-read them on reload, and keep the last good version on
-  a parse error.
-- Global instruction text goes in the config root `AGENTS.md`; OMP (hoshi-omp)
-  accepts but ignores the `instructions` key. Custom agent prompts replace the
-  provider base prompt, so shared harness rules must live in `AGENTS.md`.
+## Context and UI
 
-## Checklist
+- `context` receives a copy of outgoing messages; edits do not change stored history. Preserve user instructions and tool-call/result pairing. Summary/compaction requests have separate lifecycle coverage.
+- `message_end` can fire once per model step. Distinguish completed user work from intermediate tool rounds and respect `willContinue` on `agent_end`.
+- Gate terminal rendering with `ctx.mode === "tui"`. Headless children cannot approve interactive actions; no-op UI responses are not approvals.
+- Use managed context timers and dispose resources owned by the extension. Report errors without logging credentials, prompts or raw provider response bodies.
 
-- [ ] `bun install` done; pins match `opencode --version`.
-- [ ] Typecheck and tests pass before saving into a live setup.
-- [ ] `GET /api/plugin` shows the plugin `active`; effective state checked via
-      `/api/agent` or the relevant endpoint.
-- [ ] Only processes you started were stopped.
+## Verification
+
+Run focused tests and `bun run typecheck`, then validate with the real OMP `loadExtensions` loader and an isolated `createAgentSession`. The repository's `bun run smoke` and `bun scripts/mcp-smoke.ts` cover installed hooks, discovery and local MCPs.
+
+For routing changes, use a fake transport or test provider and inspect the outgoing request. For UI changes, inspect a temporary named terminal session and stop only that session. A policy-unit test alone does not prove loader, lifecycle, persistence, wire format or UI behavior.
+
+Verify the installed repository and launcher after copying a change. Report local test evidence separately from behavior that still requires provider sign-in.
